From 9b9f4cd2dcdbbc5221215c88433807d0a2039ec0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:13:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 69/91] Industry: Crucible bill of materials, research and copy
 times, remote install range

- Base materials are the product's invTypeMaterials less the recycled T1 item's.  They take the blueprint's waste (wasteFactor / (1 + ME), or x (1 - ME) below 0) and the character's (Production Efficiency), each rounded on its own a run.  Everything else in ramTypeRequirements is an extra material with no waste.  The show info lists and ship insurance values use the same base materials.
- The assembly line's material multiplier (1.1 in advanced arrays, 1.2 in the rapid equipment array) is sent as it is and goes on everything.
- Materials needed are checked by type, summed over base and extra.
- ME and PE research take the blueprint's base time a level, as before Crius, with no cap at 10 (127, the column's limit).  Copy time is in proportion to the copy's runs.  Times use the character's attributes, so Metallurgy, Research, Science, Industry and the Beancounter implants count (Metallurgy used to make ME research slower).  The copy time no longer wraps at 65535 seconds.
- Any reverse engineering line takes relics (the experimental laboratory's had nothing listed).
- Jobs in another station need Supply Chain Management or Scientific Networking:  the system at 1, 5 jumps at 2, 10 at 3, 20 at 4, the region at 5.
- The installation fee is refunded if the job cannot be saved.
